The test file shows the exact call being wrapped in `try/except`: `optimizers.SGD(learning_rate=0.1, clipnorm=1.0, clipvalue=0.2)`. It stores the exception as `type(e).__name__` and `str(e)`. Keras optimizer construction rejects setting more than one clipping mode at once, so passing both `clipnorm` and `clipvalue` raises a `ValueError`, and the message reports that only one of `clipnorm`, `clipvalue`, and `global_clipnorm` can be set, along with the received values.

## Answer
{"exception_message":"Only one of `clipnorm`, `clipvalue` and `global_clipnorm` can be set. Received: clipnorm=1.0, clipvalue=0.2, global_clipnorm=None","exception_type":"ValueError"}
